# A callable held by a field of a nested body is no binding after that body:
# the name is not declared where the call stands, and the call is refused.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
int: c 1
if: c = 1
    h2: make2 100
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: h2(1 2); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
